# Known entries, one JSON object per line. See tally_eval/dataset.py for the field reference.
#
# The reference numbers are seed estimates from common published values (USDA-style entries for
# whole foods, published nutrition data for branded items), rounded to the precision anyone
# would actually claim. They are a starting point and not gospel: where you disagree with one,
# edit it here — the whole harness reads this file, so a corrected reference propagates to every
# result immediately. Bands are deliberately wide; see CALORIE_TOLERANCE.
#
# Exercise references assume the body weight named on the case, since energy burned scales with
# body mass. They carry wider bands than food because the spread across published MET tables is
# genuinely that large.

